        {
          "title": "1.2 Numbers 20–100",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "title": "Tens and Compound Numbers",
              "weight": 3,
              "content": [
                {
                  "order": 1,
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "{\"time\":1700001003000,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"yY9zZ0aA1b\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"The tens in English follow a clear pattern ending in <b>-ty</b>:\"}},{\"id\":\"bB2cC3dD4e\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"<b>20</b> — twenty\",\"<b>30</b> — thirty\",\"<b>40</b> — forty\",\"<b>50</b> — fifty\",\"<b>60</b> — sixty\",\"<b>70</b> — seventy\",\"<b>80</b> — eighty\",\"<b>90</b> — ninety\",\"<b>100</b> — one hundred\"]}},{\"id\":\"eE5fF6gG7h\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"For numbers in between, we combine tens and units with a hyphen:\"}},{\"id\":\"hH8iI9jJ0k\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"21 = twenty-<b>one</b>\",\"35 = thirty-<b>five</b>\",\"47 = forty-<b>seven</b>\",\"99 = ninety-<b>nine</b>\"]}}],\"version\":\"2.31.4\"}"
                },
                {
                  "order": 2,
                  "type": "audio",
                  "content": {
